{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>With bitter herbs they shall eat it.</b> One of the sages of Spain said: It is known that moisture prevails in the land of Egypt because of the waters of the Nile, and because no rain falls there, for the air is always humid. Therefore their custom was to eat many kinds of bitter herbs at every table, from greens and mustard. And even if an Egyptian had only bread alone, bitter herbs would always be on his table to dip the bread in, for they are a remedy for their air. But we will rely on the view of our ancient predecessors, of blessed memory, who explained to us that the bitter herbs are a remembrance of \"they made their lives bitter\" (Exodus 1:14)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:27.166393386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}